CHECK:UNNECESSARY_PARENTHESES: Unnecessary parentheses around 'prev_stack->entries[i].from != cur_stack->entries[j].from'
#235: FILE: tools/perf/util/machine.c:2335:
+		if ((prev_stack->entries[i].from != cur_stack->entries[j].from) ||
+		    (prev_stack->entries[i].to != cur_stack->entries[j].to) ||
+		    (prev_stack->entries[i].flags_value != cur_stack->entries[j].flags_value))

Parentheses are not required in the following cases:

  1. Function pointer uses::

      (foo->bar)();

    could be::

      foo->bar();

  2. Comparisons in if::

      if ((foo->bar) && (foo->baz))
      if ((foo == bar))

    could be::

      if (foo->bar && foo->baz)
      if (foo == bar)

  3. addressof/dereference single Lvalues::

      &(foo->bar)
      *(foo->bar)

    could be::

      &foo->bar
      *foo->bar

